  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 142 PM CDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nThe upper-level ridge will continue to shift westward over the\nDesert Southwest into Wednesday. Isolated to scattered showers and\nthunderstorms developing over the higher terrain of New Mexico may\nmove into the southeast New Mexico Plains and the Permian Basin\nWednesday evening into late Wednesday night within the\nnorthwesterly flow aloft. Isolated to scattered showers and\nthunderstorms may develop over the region again along the eastern\nfringe of the upper ridge on Thursday. The ridge will build back\nto the east Friday through the weekend, so expect a return to\nmostly dry conditions except for a few thunderstorm in the higher\nterrain areas of our western CWA on Friday. Temperatures remain\nhot through the weekend, but may only range in the upper 90s to\naround 103 degrees for most Friday through Sunday.",
